  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WAF African Climate Caravans to COP27</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Across Africa, communities, countries, entire eco-systems are paying the price of global climate inaction. The people who are most impacted, yet least responsible have something to say about it. Their experiences, their aspirations, and their solutions matter. That is why the most polluting governments across the world have a duty of care to listen and act. In the face of the climate crisis, the African Climate Caravans are a catalyst for the demands of African people on  adaptation, climate finance, loss and damage,  andmitigation. The Caravans seek to make the perspectives, agency and action of affected communities heard at national, continental,and global levels. They do this at the occasion of the &#x2018;African COP&#x2019;: the UNFCCC climate summit COP27 that is to take place in November at Sharm-el-Sheikh, Egypt.
The African Climate Caravans campaign  has emerged organically to support collective action, movement building, awareness  raising,  joint campaigning as well as highlighting actions, agency, and  adaptation. The uptake and spread of the African Climate Caravans grew exponentially in the last months from a handful of countries in West Africa, led by regional network Jeunes Volontaires pour l&#x2019;Environnement(JVE) and Oxfam, to mobilisation and influencing by local partners in 20+ countries.
The support will allow for the convening of the Caravans around and influencing campaign during the of the African Union Presidency gathering in Senegal October 3-7, 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
